Architecture: arm64
Depends: aurora-sep, libpam-runtime, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: cryptsetup-bin
Suggests: dracut
Description: Unlock LUKS2 volumes with the Apple Secure Enclave
 aurora-sep-cryptenroll enrolls this Mac's Secure Enclave as an unlock method
 of a LUKS2 volume, like systemd-cryptenroll --tpm2-device=auto does with a
 TPM. The keyslot secret is wrapped by a kernel trusted key that the apple_sep
 driver seals, and the libcryptsetup token plugin lets cryptsetup and
 systemd-cryptsetup unlock enrolled volumes without a passphrase. The
 passphrase keyslot is always kept. Nothing is enrolled by installing this
 package.
 .
 aurora-sep-fde unlocks a volume with a user's password, checked by the
 Secure Enclave (the FileVault model), and pam_aurora_sep_fde keeps the disk
 password equal to the login password when it changes. The 90aurora-sep
 dracut module opens enrolled volumes, the root volume included, in the
 initramfs.
